{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"82787ea854b988cb","type":"text","text":"[[Noble Houses.canvas]]\n\n[[Aralia Lumiere.canvas]]\n\n#NPC #Volstarian_Dynasty ","x":-880,"y":-660,"width":402,"height":146},
		{"id":"ca76b22f666b121e","x":-886,"y":-480,"width":816,"height":540,"type":"text","text":"Azest Thelyss was once a great mage in the empire of Askain before it became the corrupt nation it has become today.\n\nHouse Thelyss was the head house of arcane practice using Dunamancy.\n\nShe worked with all of the higher-ups of old Askain including Cassian's Father Gabriel. \n\nShe will recognize Cassian if she sees him and will have general information on his dad but might not be entirely willing to share. \n\nAzest made her way to Yormindar after Askains fall in an attempt to gather a large amount of Residuum to use to possible cure the people of their mind control and destroy those who influence them. While in the bottom of the mine she was taken by the Lolth sworn drow and turned into a scout for them. \n\nShe does not have any memory of what happened while being mind controlled by the Drow but is willing to assist the party in destroying them. When she first awakens she will not have all of her memories intact but will eventually come back to full strength.\n\n\nHer responsibilities in Askain were to utilize a device known as The Dreamer's Heart. She used this device to harness both time and gravity magic.\n\nGab wanted to the magic from it and tried to get help from the continent of Unhileg to take it from Azest but in the process started the war of old\n"},
		{"id":"83082bcedd0f10d3","x":-886,"y":100,"width":663,"height":930,"type":"text","text":"The Veridian:\n\nRenamed after the now Deceased ex-wife of Azest Thelyss. The Veridian is made up of three parts.\n\nThe main deck:\n\nWide purple sails blow in the wind on top of a wooden deck that is about 100 feet from front to back. There are two arcane cannons one on each side of the ship. There is a double staircase that curves to a top deck with the ships height, speed and directional controls this is all done through one arcane orb. In the center of the staircase is a door that leads below.\n\nArcane Cannon:\n\nDC 20 Arcana check to fire then an attack roll adding the users intelligence modifier to the roll. On a hit the cannon deals 10d10 Force damage and the creature it hits must make a DC 15 strength check or fall prone.\n\nThe Round Table Quarter:\n\nJust below the main deck is an open room that spans almost the entirety of the ship at the back of the ship is a doorway to the captains quarters and in the center of this room is a round table with a map of the Volstarian Dynasty in the center of it, each city or fortress is labelled on the map but some locations in Armount are still unknown. The room is lit by artifical arcane torch light that glows ember orange and there are 8 chairs around the table. Off to the right side is a staircase that leads below.\n\nThe Captains quarters (Azests room):\n\nAs you enter through the door directly across from you there is no wall just two pillars that hold the upper deck sturdy and an open balcony behind a beautiful bed made of gold frame and lavender purple cloths with a mosquito net covering the bed. On the left side of the room there is a dresser with a mirror on it mad of mahogany and on the right side there is a tall wardrobe. The balcony has a wooden railing that wraps around it and in its center is a table with two chairs two wine glasses and an open bottle.\n\nThe sleeping quarters:\nA hallway of doors that all lead to bedrooms. Within each bedroom there is a mirror a bed a dresser a closet and a circular window.\n\n"},
		{"id":"7f41134b50830b92","x":-180,"y":100,"width":587,"height":846,"type":"text","text":"Veridian Thyless:\n\nA half-drow woman who was the same age as Azest. Veridian was from continent known as Lanavier and the country of Lanvi a costal nation known for its beautiful oceans and beaches. She left Lanvi when she was 60 years old and ended up in Askain to research about magic and hopefully be able to one day become a teacher to students in an academy. \n\nVeridian loved children and wanted to give back to the world, when she saw the people on the council of Askain fight she would always say her piece even though not being a member everyone respected her for her kindness and generosity. People used to say her and Azest made the perfect match, Azest a arcana fanatic who loves to show off. Veridian a kind woman who knew how to shut people down, calm them down and humble them, but whenever she would speak the entire room would go silent. She was a natural born leader and teacher who devoted her life to her students and wife. Veridian was murdered in front of Azests eyes in their bedroom by Verazanoth, he baited Azest into a trap then took his chance to go after Veridian and when Azest arrived he told her to give him the secrets to Dunamis or he would kill Veridian. Before Azest could even speak Veridian attempted a spell that would kill both her and Verazanoth, he stopped it by cutting of her head and throwing it to Azest taunting her, telling her that there is nothing she can do to stop him or his God. Seeking revenge Azest traveled to Volstar and spent 10 years training their military then she went to Yormindar and spent another year gathering allies and attempting to gain access to the mines. Eventually she was given access right when Askain fell when she attempted to return home she was interrupted by Gabriel Draemont who told her that he told Verazanoth about Dunamis and Veridian as a way to get to Azest. Gabriel told her that he wanted the power of Dunamis for himself and reached out to Verazanoth for help. A battle broke out between them in the dessert before Xroas and before it could end they both watched a light beam by them Azest took the chance to disappear and go back to the residuum mines to acquire the power necessary to take down the Unhileg. The rest is known.\n"},
		{"id":"366b651c8810491f","x":-25,"y":-480,"width":432,"height":270,"type":"text","text":"Azest's current motivations:\n\nGet revenge on Verazanoth.\n\nFollow in Veridians footsteps and teach at the Hellos academy. \n\nFree Askain of the Unhileg. \n\nFigure out how she truly feels about Aralia and make sure what happens history does not repeat itself.\n"},
		{"id":"704d8c9a9b58d607","x":-460,"y":-660,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Age: 140\n"},
